{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact Head A head f8c71ba2a83297051681b3031c04fab36a4d33ed on builder/head-a-register-values-20261114, all 5 artifacts, for request 56c48bc9 under implementation promise 9df71a88 and my promise f520fb99. The demo file is right. The lending and grow files list a retired register beside the new one, so the head does not name what those Workers run. I reached this finding before I read planner act aa2d1b9e, and I agree with its repair.\n\nRequired change: each of the three files lists the new root alone.\n\n- `wrangler.lending.jsonc` gains `INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES` with the retired `sc_c67lq575…` and the new `sc_psbin3zi…`. `wrangler.grow.jsonc` gains it with the retired `sc_yatkl7ku…` and the new `sc_wmtd3fkl…`.\n- The running Workers have no such variable. Plan 036 line 138 adds `INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES:[\"$REG\"]` on dap-demo alone, and END 53d5a148 reports the variable on dap-demo alone. Without the variable, the list is the current root alone (`installed-registers.ts:7`).\n- A listed root grants authority. `creation-lineage.ts:143` admits a creation chain whose root register is in `register.scopes`. A deployment of this head would list each retired register again as a creation root on lending and grow. `docs/deploy.md:327` states the opposite: \"The identifier cutover uses `--only` because the service does not read rooms of the retired roots.\"\n- The commands followed request 9d3bbe4c exactly. The request names `--only` for demo alone, so the defect sits in the instruction, as aa2d1b9e says.\n- Repair as aa2d1b9e says: run the script once for each Worker from main 0ad4aa91, each with `--only`, and show that no retired scope ID stays in any file. The config change after the gate is outside the follow-up rule of `docs/evidence-filing.md`, so the new head needs its own gate.\n\nFor the later script question in aa2d1b9e: keeping the old primary root by default turns every rotation into a widening of creation authority unless the operator remembers `--only`. A rotation that retires its old register is the common case for this helper. I recommend that the helper require either `--only` or an explicit `--keep` and refuse when neither is given.\n\nWhat holds at this head, and carries to the next one:\n\n- Values. Each `REGISTER_SCOPE` and `ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope` equals the scope in END 53d5a148: lending `sc_psbin3zi…`, grow `sc_wmtd3fkl…`, demo `sc_dtqcta4h…`. The demo offer carries genesis `sha256:e1d53ac5…`, the origin https://dap-demo.inguz.workers.dev, deployment `dap-demo` and `platform:register@28`, as END 53d5a148 names. No tracked `DEPLOYMENT` is added to demo. The recorded argv of the three runs match these values.\n- Merge. `git merge-tree` of 0ad4aa91 and 04d556aa gives a0cbda3e, which equals the tree of merge d720ae65 and the gated tree. After d720ae65, only the note and the manifest change. Outside `notes/`, the head equals the gated source. Git records mode 100644 for all three files.\n- Evidence. The manifest hashes to 497aa347, as the request states. All 109 listed files match their SHA-256 and byte counts. `SHA256SUMS` verifies in the script, gate and documentation directories, and those checksum files hash to ace0ac97, 30b43c20 and 74ab959a. The gate at 04d556aa ends \"gate passed\" with no timeout line. All 79 samples read AC Power, and every reading shows powermode 0. The host's `pmset -g log` shows no sleep or wake from 02:00 to 04:00 EST.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 4 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: the helper's output is the right shape for Head A. The required change concerns which roots the head lists, not the mechanism.\n\nSecurity: the required change above. Listing a retired register widens creation authority on two production Workers beyond what they run today.\n\nSimplification: no required change. See the recommendation on the helper's default above.\n\nThis verdict authorizes no landing or deployment. The hold on `deploy.mjs` for grow, lending and demo stays.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:98a33489d6f8d29cfe9dc28d709b5ed4ad3294bb","binding":"assigned","head":"f8c71ba2a83297051681b3031c04fab36a4d33ed","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f520fb9920232e1650c0cc4a134c946568c22328\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:aa2d1b9eec4352fa3cd14829505220ae3dd032f4\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9df71a88b3722b085ba7cf747168c54996a4bbd6\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:332f5f9e9828b860afc6a7745a228e06a4c5bf62","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}